{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-20061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a)$, if $3a\\cdot (6b\\times c)=90.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-20061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a\\cdot (6b\\times c) & =90 \\\\ 3\\cdot 6\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =90 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a) & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-20061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65d3b89c237524eb311f49ccf0549c46eb1895b66967de85d0b66db5f1370d2d"} {"question" "q-20061" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-20061" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-20061" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-73462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨3,1,2⟩$, $q=⟨1,-2,1⟩$ and $r=⟨4,1,-2⟩.$ Find $r\\cdot (q\\times p).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-73462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $r\\cdot (q\\times p)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $r,$ $q,$ and $p.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot (q\\times p) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4((-2)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-(1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3)-2(1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-20+1-14 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-73462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65d3b89c237524eb311f49ccf0549c46eb1895b66967de85d0b66db5f1370d2d"} {"question" "q-73462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-73462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-14"] ["math" "-20"] ["math" "-30"] ["math" "-33"] ["math" "10"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-73462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-33"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-128356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a),$ if $b\\times c=⟨6,-1,3⟩$ and $a=⟨3,5,-4⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-128356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨3,5,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =3\\cdot 6+5\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =18-5-12 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-128356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65d3b89c237524eb311f49ccf0549c46eb1895b66967de85d0b66db5f1370d2d"} {"question" "q-128356" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-128356" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-128356" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-317312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2,-1,3⟩$, $b=⟨0,4,1⟩$ and $c=⟨-2,1,5⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-317312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\,(4\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 1)\\,-\\,(-1)\\,(0\\cdot 5-1\\cdot (-2))\\,+\\,3\\,(0\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =2\\,(19)\\,-\\,(-1)\\,(2)\\,+\\,3\\,(8) \\\\  & =38+2+24 \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-317312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65d3b89c237524eb311f49ccf0549c46eb1895b66967de85d0b66db5f1370d2d"} {"question" "q-317312" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-317312" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "64"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-317316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨0,2,5⟩$, $b=⟨3,1,0⟩$ and $c=⟨4,-1,-2⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-317316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\,(1\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot (-1))\\,-\\,2\\,(3\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 4)\\,+\\,5\\,(3\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =0(-2)\\,-\\,2\\,(-6)\\,+\\,5\\,(-7) \\\\  & =0+12-35 \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-317316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65d3b89c237524eb311f49ccf0549c46eb1895b66967de85d0b66db5f1370d2d"} {"question" "q-317316" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"} {"question" "q-317316" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-23"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043174/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cd5d873cadcaae8c73b79385e5db9f78ab243e6180f7ff4d19b626b1d34f7f9"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1616 